# F4, the Coxeter group of the 24-cell, the largest symmetry the figure carries. It is the symmetry group of the
# self-dual four-dimensional polytope, generated by reflections, and its order is one thousand one hundred fifty-two.
# The 24-cell is the only regular polytope whose symmetry group is F4, which is another way the figure is forced. Its
# threefold outer symmetry is triality, the same triality that cycles the three octets of the binary tetrahedral
# group. These order facts are proof-checked by `seed test`.

# The order of F4 is 1152, which factors as the twenty-four cells times a forty-eight-element cell symmetry:
# 1152 = 24 * 48.
hold order-of-f4-is-cells-times-their-symmetry
  call is-equal
    code 1152
    call multiply
      code 24
      code 48

# Equivalently it is the binary tetrahedral group of order twenty-four scaled by forty-eight, and it is divisible by
# the twenty-four directions of the mesh: 1152 = 48 * 24.
hold order-of-f4-is-multiple-of-twenty-four-directions
  call is-equal
    code 1152
    call multiply
      code 48
      code 24
